# A device build writes DEVELOPMENT_TEAM into the generated Xcode project from
# APPLE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM, and that project is committed — so an Apple team id
# lands in the working tree every time anyone builds for a phone, in a public
# repo, waiting to be committed by accident.
#
# A clean filter strips it on the way into the index. The file still diffs
# normally for every other change; only this one line never reaches a commit.
# Turn it on once per clone:
#
#     git config filter.strip-apple-team.clean "sed '/DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = /d'"
#     git config filter.strip-apple-team.smudge cat
#
# Without that config git leaves the file alone, so a clone that never builds
# for iOS needs nothing.
src-tauri/gen/apple/pigeon.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj filter=strip-apple-team
